00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:06.260
LILIANA YU: Welcome to
the first Cloud Labs

00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:08.570
episode on the GCP
Essentials Quest

00:00:08.570 --> 00:00:11.600
on Qwiklabs, Creating
a Virtual Machine.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:14.210
In this quest, you get your
first hands-on experience

00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:17.060
with Google Cloud, get
comfortable with the basics,

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:20.090
like spinning up a VM and
configuring key infrastructure

00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:22.850
tools through working with
more advanced Stackdriver

00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:24.460
and Kubernetes concepts.

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:26.790
You'll work your way
through each lab on Qwiklabs

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:30.230
until you have completed your
quest and received your badge.

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:33.850
You do not need a Google Cloud
Platform account or project.

00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:36.650
An account, project,
and associated resources

00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:39.110
are provided to you
as part of each lab.

00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:41.170
Let's see what this
lab is about then.

00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:43.940
Google Compute Engine lets
you create virtual machines

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:45.930
running different
operating systems,

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:47.960
including multiple
flavors of Linux--

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:51.730
Debian, Ubuntu, Red
Hat, and CoreOS--

00:00:51.730 --> 00:00:54.500
and Windows Server on
Google infrastructure.

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:56.720
You can run thousands
of virtual CPUs

00:00:56.720 --> 00:00:59.810
on a system that has
been designed to be fast

00:00:59.810 --> 00:01:03.860
and to offer strong
consistency of performance.

00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:05.570
In this hands-on
lab, you'll learn

00:01:05.570 --> 00:01:08.570
how to create a virtual machine
instance using a Google Cloud

00:01:08.570 --> 00:01:12.650
Platform console and using
the G-Cloud command line,

00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:15.920
create a virtual machine with
the G-Cloud command line,

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:19.580
deploy a web server and connect
it to a virtual machine.

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:21.350
It's helpful if you
have familiarity

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:25.310
with standard Linux text
editors, such as Vim, VMAX,

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:26.570
or Nano.

00:01:26.570 --> 00:01:28.790
Google Compute Engine
is the foundation

00:01:28.790 --> 00:01:32.390
to Google Cloud platform's
infrastructure as a service.

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:36.920
Next up on our quest is Compute
Engine, Qwik Start, Windows.

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:39.290
A quest is a series
of related labs

00:01:39.290 --> 00:01:41.900
that form a learning
path on Qwiklabs.

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:44.510
Completing this quest
earns you this badge

00:01:44.510 --> 00:01:46.340
to recognize your achievement.

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:47.750
Good luck and have fun!

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:51.400
